
Text 2: Surveys in three rewilded London parks found that visits rose after mowing stopped, and that respondents most often described the meadows as ''alive''. Perceptions of safety were unchanged from the pre-rewilding baseline.', 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the criticism described in Text 1?', '[{"key":"A","text":"By conceding that unmanaged parkland does reduce visitor numbers"},{"key":"B","text":"By noting that the predicted loss of welcome is not what the survey data show"},{"key":"C","text":"By arguing that safety matters less than biodiversity"},{"key":"D","text":"By claiming that residents cannot judge the quality of parkland"}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'Text 2 reports higher visits and unchanged safety perceptions, which directly contradicts Text 1''s prediction that unmanaged parks feel less welcoming. Choice C is tempting but Text 2 never ranks the two values; it simply reports that the feared cost did not appear.') on conflict (id) do nothing;

Text 2: A study of relocations found that remote workers overwhelmingly moved to a small number of mid-sized cities that already had high amenity scores and rising rents. Rural counties gained almost no net workers.', 'Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Text 2 provides an empirical qualification of the mechanism Text 1 describes."},{"key":"B","text":"Text 2 offers a historical precedent for the trend Text 1 predicts."},{"key":"C","text":"Text 2 endorses Text 1''s conclusion using different reasoning."},{"key":"D","text":"Text 2 disputes Text 1''s definition of remote work."}]'::jsonb, 'A', null, 'Text 1 claims remote work spreads opportunity widely; Text 2''s relocation data show the gains concentrating in a few already-attractive cities, narrowing rather than rejecting the claim. Choice C is wrong because the data cut against, not for, the broad redistribution Text 1 forecasts.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• Cochineal is a red dye made from scale insects.
• It was farmed in Oaxaca before Spanish contact.
• By 1600 it was the second most valuable export from New Spain after silver.
• Synthetic red dyes displaced it in the 1870s.

The student wants to emphasise cochineal''s commercial importance in the colonial period.', 'Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Cochineal, a red dye made from scale insects, was farmed in Oaxaca long before Spanish contact."},{"key":"B","text":"By 1600 cochineal, a dye made from scale insects, was New Spain''s second most valuable export after silver."},{"key":"C","text":"Cochineal, once farmed in Oaxaca, was displaced by synthetic red dyes in the 1870s."},{"key":"D","text":"Synthetic dyes of the 1870s replaced a red dye that had been made from scale insects."}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'Only choice B carries the export-ranking note, which is the one detail that establishes commercial importance in the colonial period. Choice A is accurate but speaks to antiquity, and choices C and D emphasise the dye''s later decline.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• The Antikythera mechanism is a geared bronze device recovered from a shipwreck in 1901.
• X-ray tomography in 2006 revealed at least 30 interlocking gears.
• It modelled the positions of the sun and moon and predicted eclipses.
• No comparably complex geared device is known for the next thousand years.

The student wants to explain to an audience unfamiliar with the mechanism why it is historically remarkable.', 'Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"The Antikythera mechanism was recovered from a shipwreck in 1901 and studied with X-ray tomography in 2006."},{"key":"B","text":"With at least 30 interlocking gears, the mechanism modelled the sun and moon and predicted eclipses — and nothing so complex is known for the next thousand years."},{"key":"C","text":"X-ray tomography in 2006 revealed that the Antikythera mechanism contains at least 30 interlocking gears."},{"key":"D","text":"Recovered in 1901, the Antikythera mechanism is a geared bronze device that modelled the positions of the sun and moon."}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'Remarkableness needs both the device''s capability and the fact that it had no successor for a millennium, and only choice B pairs them. Choice C gives the gear count but leaves the reader with no standard of comparison to judge it against.') on conflict (id) do nothing;

Text 2: Since 2019 the museum has returned 27 objects and reports that loan agreements negotiated alongside each return have brought 63 objects into its galleries, most never previously exhibited in Europe.', 'Based on the texts, how does the evidence in Text 2 bear on the concern raised in Text 1?', '[{"key":"A","text":"It confirms that returns reduce the size of collections."},{"key":"B","text":"It suggests returns can be paired with arrangements that expand, rather than shrink, what is on display."},{"key":"C","text":"It shows that global audiences prefer to see objects in their countries of origin."},{"key":"D","text":"It demonstrates that loan agreements are more expensive than acquisitions."}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'The museum returned 27 objects but gained 63 on loan, so the feared depletion did not occur. Choice A reads only the first half of the data and ignores the loans that followed each return.') on conflict (id) do nothing;

Text 2: Corpus studies of speech directed at young children find it is far more repetitive and far better formed than earlier researchers assumed, with common constructions recurring thousands of times per month.', 'Which choice best describes how Text 2 relates to the argument in Text 1?', '[{"key":"A","text":"It challenges a premise of the argument rather than its conclusion."},{"key":"B","text":"It provides an additional example of the phenomenon the argument explains."},{"key":"C","text":"It agrees with the argument but questions its significance."},{"key":"D","text":"It shows that the argument rests on a mathematical error."}]'::jsonb, 'A', null, 'Text 1''s reasoning depends on the input being fragmentary; Text 2 attacks precisely that premise while saying nothing directly about innateness. Choice C is wrong because Text 2 does not accept the argument — it removes one of its supports.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• The Tabula Peutingeriana is a medieval copy of a Roman road map.
• It is 6.75 metres long and only 34 centimetres tall.
• Distances along roads are accurate; the shapes of coastlines are heavily distorted.
• It was designed to be rolled and carried.

The student wants to explain why the map''s distortions were not a flaw.', 'Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"The Tabula Peutingeriana is 6.75 metres long but only 34 centimetres tall."},{"key":"B","text":"Because it was made to be rolled up and used for travel along roads, the map keeps road distances accurate and lets coastlines distort."},{"key":"C","text":"The Tabula Peutingeriana is a medieval copy of a Roman original."},{"key":"D","text":"Coastlines on the Tabula Peutingeriana are heavily distorted."}]'::jsonb, 'B', null, 'Justifying the distortion requires linking the map''s purpose — portable route-finding — to what it chose to keep accurate, and only choice B does both. Choice D states the distortion without offering any reason it was acceptable.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
• Wangari Maathai founded the Green Belt Movement in Kenya in 1977.
• The movement paid rural women small sums for each seedling that survived.
• More than 50 million trees have been planted through it.
• Maathai received the Nobel Peace Prize in 2004.

The student wants to explain the movement''s design to an audience interested in what made it effective.', 'Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Wangari Maathai, who received the Nobel Peace Prize in 2004, founded the Green Belt Movement in 1977."},{"key":"B","text":"The Green Belt Movement, founded in Kenya in 1977, has planted more than 50 million trees."},{"key":"C","text":"The Green Belt Movement paid rural women for each seedling that survived, tying income to the trees'' long-term success."},{"key":"D","text":"Wangari Maathai founded the Green Belt Movement in Kenya in 1977 and won the Nobel Peace Prize in 2004."}]'::jsonb, 'C', null, 'A question about design and effectiveness calls for the incentive structure — payment on survival rather than on planting — which only choice C reports and interprets. Choice B gives the result but not the mechanism that produced it.') on conflict (id) do nothing;
